			"notes": "## New Features\n\n- Bundled every supported Minecraft version (1.20.1, 1.21.1, 1.21.11) and loader (Fabric, Forge, NeoForge) into a single release\n- The Minecraft 1.21.11 NeoForge build is published as alpha\n\n\n## Fixes\n\n- Fixed ModernUI's tooltip drop shadow clipping nearby GUI elements such as JEI's item list, Create: Aeronautics' creative-tab banner and HUD banners. ModernUI draws the shadow as part of the same SDF quad as the background and inflates it by `shadowRadius * 1.2`, and those translucent pixels wrote depth. Anything drawn afterwards inside the inflated shadow rectangle then failed the depth test and vanished. The compat now zeroes `sShadowRadius`/`sShadowAlpha` for the single `drawRoundedBackground` call and restores the user's ModernUI settings afterwards, so nothing outside the opaque panel writes depth.\n\n\n## Known Issues\n\n- **NeoForge (alpha)**: the client hangs at the loading screen on macOS because the ModernUI fork initializes AWT/AppKit from NeoForge's mod-loading worker thread. Launch with `-Djava.awt.headless=true` as a workaround.\n- **NeoForge (alpha)**: the built-in `vibrant_tooltips` resource pack does not load, so tooltips fall back to the default style."
		},
