			"notes": "## New Features\n\n- Added support for Minecraft 1.21.11 on Fabric and NeoForge\n- Renders ModernUI's rounded SDF tooltip background through the deferred GUI render-state system\n- Uses obscure-tooltips' soft white header separator to match ModernUI's rounded background\n\n\n## Fixes\n\n- Fixed tooltip routing on 1.21.11 by hiding ModernUI's tooltip option at priority 0 and rendering obscure-tooltips directly, so ModernUI's own handler falls through\n- Restored the ModernUI tooltip option before the render state uniforms are bound, so the rounded background is actually drawn\n\n\n## Known Issues (NeoForge alpha)\n\nThe NeoForge build is alpha:\n\n- The client hangs at the loading screen on macOS: the ModernUI fork initializes AWT/AppKit from NeoForge's mod-loading worker thread, which deadlocks on macOS. Launch with `-Djava.awt.headless=true` as a workaround.\n- The built-in `vibrant_tooltips` resource pack does not load on NeoForge, so tooltips fall back to the default style."
		}
